      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-04-13_WidnesExaminer_art0060" n="art0060">
        <head>Joint Serrice of Primitive Methodists.</head>
        <p>Joint Serrice of Primitive Methodists.</p>
        <p>On Good Friday, a joint service of the Colborne- street Baptist Church and Legh-street Primitive Methodist Church was conducted by the Rev. W. Cooper in the Legh-street Church. Suitable hymns were sung and appropriate lessons read and the Rev. H. Ogden of olborne-street preached an excellent sermon taking for his text "And they crucified Him." The rev, gentleman pointed out that it was not the rabble of the day who crucified Christ so much as the church itself,that the rabble and Roman soldiers were mere agents and tools in the hands of the Pharisees and the leaders of the church. Even in the crucifixion the Master triumphed, and the rabble who shouted for His crucifixion gave the key to the real triumph of the Lord and Master, They shouted "He saved others, Himself Ile cannot save." The triumph of Christ was in voluntary suffet ing for the masses of mankind.</p>
        <p>FRODSHAM CHURCH. MEMORIAL TO THE LATE RECTOR. The vestry meeting was held on Easter Monday, the Rev R L Mann (curate-in-charge), presiding. The officers for the ensuing year were appointed as follows: Vicar's warden' Mr W N Hutchings ; parishioners' warden, Mr J Wilkinson ; side3men (Parish Church), Messrs .1 C Cragg, W Burrows, R II Dutton, W A Lewis, H Andrews, %V Unsworth ; Iron Church, Messrs (3 Garner, C Ormsby, S 0 Woods ; churchyard committee, Messrs J Garner, C E Linaker, J 0 Aston, J C Caw', and the two wardens ; lay represent itives, Messrs W N Hutchings and T D Timmins ; hon. auditor, Mr T D Timmins. A. vote of condolence was paszei with Mrs Blogg at the loss of her husband, Canon H B Blogg, and it was resolved that a permanent memorial in the form of a stained glass window be put in the Parish Church, and that the following committe( the scheme: Messrs T D Garner, H Tilly, C E Lui Hutchings, J J VVilkinson, W Myers).</p>
        <p>N</p>
      </div>
