        <p>tion." Doubting Thomas was referred to as a warning to doubting minds ; a doubting person could not be a great help to his followers. A serviceable limn must be whole-hearted and true, and full of faith and zeal. Mr Himsworth and Mr. Cotton took part in the meet- ing. the brethren took up a collection for the Mayor's I ,istress Fund and it realised £l. The Secretary (Mr Farrar) commented upon the closing of the great strike, which, he said, ought to fill everyone's heart with thankfulness. The meeting closed with the singing of " Praise God from Whom all blessings flow."</p>
