      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-04-13_WidnesExaminer_art0070" n="art0070">
        <head>REV. MICHAEL DOWLEY.</head>
        <p>THE REV. MICHAEL DOWLEY.</p>
        <p>Expressions of regret at the departure of the Rev. Father Dowley from Warrington are heard on all sides at present, particularly from the congregation of the Sacred Heart Church, where he has worked for the past two and a half-years. Father Dowley is recalled to his native Diocese of Waterford, and the Irish people of Warrington, generally, are regretting his removal from their midst. During his few years in town he has acted as Roman Catholic chaplain to the Workhouse and hospital, and endeared himself by his zeal and genial manner to all the officers and inmates th-re, irrespective of religion. The St. Patrick's Day concerts held in the Parr Hall for the last three years successively on the 17th March, under his direction, will not soon be forgotten, while as a preacher in the Sacred Heart Church, and on special occasions in other churches in town, Father Dowley proved himself an eloquent son of the Irish soil. The Roman Catholic poor and sick in the Workhouse and hospital will keenly feel his departure and all who aro acquainted with him pers nally feel deeply their los in his recall to Ireland. We wish him many years of happiness and success in his new sphere of work. He leaves for Waterford on Monday next.</p>
      </div>
