        <p>CIOUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. RELIEF OF DIHRESS CAUSED BY THE CO A L STRIKE. Whilst thanking the inhabitants of Warrington and , District for their generous assistance to the fund, it is with regret that I feel compelled to renew my appeal for a continuance of their support and help in increasing the fund for the above purpose. The last week has shown that the distress is not decreasing and there are many sad cases to be dealt with. Gifts of potatoes, food-stuffs, and fuel will be welcomed. Subscriptions may he paid to the Borough Treasurer, Bank House, Sankey Street, or into any of the Banks. Town Hall, Warrington, G. W. JOSEPH, 12th April, 1912. Mayor. LIST OF SUBSCRIPTIONS. l a. d. J.Crosfleld &amp; Sons, Ltd. (3rd instal) 50 0 0 Warrington Co-operative Society 1 (goods, 34d contribution) Amount collected at the Warring- ton Conservative Club (2nd instalment) : I s. d. Ji hn Cozen lO 0 0 IVilliam Fairhurst 1 1 0 James A.Rnshworth 1 1 0 Arderman James Smethurst Frederick Short 1 0 0 M. Moss H Hayes C. G. McDowell Frank Kerfeet 5s , W. Longshaw 24., and Thos. Horobin Is 0 S 0 -- 16 1 6 Rev. W. .7. Stanton Mrs. Stanton l2 10 0 Charles It'. Parker lO 10 0 J. Charlton Parr (2nd instal) lO 0 0 James Fairclough and Sons, Ltd lO 0 0 Collected at Bold-street Wesleyan Church 8 12 11 Mrs. Je hn Crosfield (Colwyn Bay) 5 5 0 Thomas Hewitt (Southport) 5 5 0 Robert Pierpoint (3rd instal) 5 0 0 Miss Milner (per week for 3 weeks) 5 0 0 Peter Stubs Ltd. Mies M. G. Ry lands 5 0 0 Vere B. Davies 5 0 0 Edward G. Davies Hon. }Minor Wilson-Patten 5 0 0 Bon. Elizabeth Wilson-Patten 5 0 0 Employees of Richmond &amp; Co ( Grappenhall Works, lat instal) 411 3 Lymm, per Rector Mrs. James Fairclough Henry Roberts (3rd instal) 3 0 0 2nd Collection, Mersey Flint Glass Works C.E. Church of Winwick Asylum • 2 5 6 Prank A. Harris 2 2 0 B. S. Townroe (2nd instalment) Mrs Rylands Lionel Fairclough 2 2 0 Mrs. R. Pierpoint (3rd instal) W. Penn Collected at United Service between Golborne 